# {{.Project}}

Scaffolded with [goforge](https://github.com/VictorTarnovski/goforge).

## Layout

- `cmd/api` — the HTTP server entrypoint.
- `cmd/ctl` — operational CLI (`{{.Project}}ctl`){{if .DB}}, including `migrate`{{end}}.
- `internal/<domain>` — one package per business domain, colocating its model, service, repository{{if .DB}}, and migration{{end}}, and HTTP handler.
- `internal/httpx` — shared HTTP kit: JSON envelopes, RFC 7807 problem details, error classification.
{{- if .DB}}
- `internal/db`, `internal/uow` — database connection and unit-of-work helpers.
- `migrations/` — goose SQL migrations, run via `{{.Project}}ctl migrate`.
{{- end}}
- `internal/authn` — OIDC bearer-token verification, applied to every request.
{{- if .HasAuthz}}
- `internal/authz` — OpenFGA permission checks.
{{- end}}
- `docs/adr/` — architecture decision records.
- `.claude/skills`, `.agents/rules` — the Go conventions this project follows, vendored at scaffold time.

## Getting started

```sh
go mod tidy
{{- if .DB}}
cp .env.example .env   # then edit DSN / OIDC /{{if .HasAuthz}}OpenFGA{{end}} settings
docker compose up -d   # starts{{if .DB}} Postgres{{end}}{{if .HasAuthz}} and OpenFGA{{end}}
go run ./cmd/ctl migrate
{{- end}}
make run
```

## Common tasks

See `Makefile` for `run`, `test`, `lint`, and{{if .DB}} `migrate`{{end}}.

## Generating a new domain

```sh
goforge generate domain <name> --fields name:string,count:int
```

Adds `internal/<name>/` as a full vertical slice{{if .DB}}, plus a migration under `migrations/`{{end}}.
